fibrosus and nucleus pulposus for intervertebral disc replacement</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>2004</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>1290</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><comment>discussion 1297-8</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15187626</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thonar</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Masuda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biological repair of intervertebral disc</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>2003</year><volume>28</volume><issue>Suppl</issue><fpage>S86</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12897480</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cassinelli</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biochemistry of intervertebral disc degeneration and the potential for gene therapy applications</article-title><source>Spine J</source><year>2001</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14588349</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helm</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gazit</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Future uses of mesenchymal stem cells in spine surgery</article-title><source>Neurosurg Focus</source><year>2005</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>E13</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16398478</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R20">